Rule 1 (The shapes of input tensors x1 and x2 must be compatible for element-wise addition)
{x1 : tensor, x2 : tensor} |= shape(x1) = shape(x2)
>>
Rule 3 (If `where` is provided, it must be a boolean tensor)
{where : tensor} |= dtype_(where) = bool
>>
Rule 7 (If `out` tensor is provided, it must have the same shape as x1 and x2 tensors)
{x1 : tensor, x2 : tensor, out : tensor} |= shape(out) = shape(x1) ∧ shape(out) = shape(x2)
>>
Rule 8 (Check if the input tensors are not empty. Number of dimensions is greater than 0.)
{x1 : tensor, x2 : tensor} |= ndim(x1) > 0 ∧ ndim(x2) > 0
>>
Rule 9 (If the type of the first argument is float16, float32, or float64, then the type of the second argument must be float16, float32, or float64 as well)
{x1 : tensor, x2 : tensor} |= if (dtype_(x1) = float16 ∨ dtype_(x1) = float32 ∨ dtype_(x1) = float64) then (dtype_(x2) = float16 ∨ dtype_(x2) = float32 ∨ dtype_(x2) = float64)
>>
Rule 10 (If the type of the first argument is complex64, complex128, then the type of the second argument must be complex64, complex128 as well)
{x1 : tensor, x2 : tensor} |= if (dtype_(x1) = complex64 ∨ dtype_(x1) = complex128) then (dtype_(x2) = complex64 ∨ dtype_(x2) = complex128)
>>
Rule 11 (If x1 is bool, x2 is bool, then out is bool)
{x1 : tensor, x2 : tensor, out : tensor} |= if (dtype_(x1) = bool ∧ dtype_(x2) = bool) then dtype_(out) = bool
>>
Rule 34 (The shape of 'where' must be the same as x1 if x1 has only one dimension and x2 is a scalar)
{x1: tensor, x2: tensor, where: tensor} |= if (ndim(x1) = 1 ∧ ndim(x2) = 0) then shape(x1) = shape(where)
>>
Rule 35 (The shape of 'where' must be the same as x2 if x2 has only one dimension and x1 is a scalar)
{x1: tensor, x2: tensor, where: tensor} |= if (ndim(x1) = 0 ∧ ndim(x2) = 1) then shape(x2) = shape(where)
>>
Rule 42 (Prevent using bool type for calculations.)
{x1: tensor, x2: tensor} |= dtype_(x1) ≠ bool ∧ dtype_(x2) ≠ bool
>>
Rule 44 (If both x1 and x2 are scalars then output is a scalar)
{x1: tensor, x2: tensor, out: tensor} |= if (ndim(x1) = 0 ∧ ndim(x2) = 0) then ndim(out) = 0
>>
Rule 48 (Check overflow for exponentiation of x1 and x2)
{x1:tensor, x2: tensor} |= (max(x1) < 709) ∧ (max(x2) < 709)
>>
Rule 53 (If x1 and x2 are both boolean tensors and `out` is provided, it must also be a boolean tensor.)
{x1: tensor, x2: tensor, out: tensor} |= if (dtype_(x1) = bool ∧ dtype_(x2) = bool) then dtype_(out) = bool
